<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assur Fernández</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assur">Assur</a> Fernández was a Castilian noble whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiro-ii-of-leon">Ramiro II of León</a> made count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monzon">Monzón</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a>, around 943. The county was created as a counterweight to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernan-gonzalez-of-castile">Fernán González of Castile</a>. His descendants, the Ansúrez family, included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ansurez">Pedro Ansúrez</a>, lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid">Valladolid</a>.</p></div>
